abstract: >-
  ASI is an evidence-driven JAX research project hillclimbing toward an
  end-to-end continual-learning agent for ongoing work and robotics. The
  project is inspired by, but not limited to, the Alberta Plan. It develops
  online adaptation, prediction, control, learned state, memory, planning, and
  fail-closed evidence tooling for non-stationary supervised and reinforcement
  learning problems. The current software does not claim state-of-the-art or
  robotics-ready performance.
